# Images dropped in the repo ROOT. This is the scratch area where screenshots
# land while reporting a visual problem -- reference renders, "here is the
# glitch" crops. They are conversation, not artefacts, and there are already a
# dozen of them. Anchored with a leading slash so images that ARE artefacts,
# under assets/ docs/ and design/, are untouched.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.gif
/*.webp
/*.bmp
/*.tif
/*.tiff

# Diagnostic renders from tools/preview_render.py. Regenerate on demand; they
# are a debugging aid, not an input to anything.
design/preview/

# The PDF embeds a 3MB copy of the PSD mockup preview alongside the artwork.
# tools/pdf_to_svg.py extracts every image it finds, but nothing consumes this
# one -- only the two logo stencils (img25, img44) are used.
design/artwork/pdf-images/img26_3000x3000.png

# Python bytecode from the tools/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Per-machine Claude Code settings: permission allowlists with absolute paths
# and session ids in them. .claude/settings.json (shared) is not ignored.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Scratch working notes from the superpowers tooling.
.superpowers/
